   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Cursor Gravity\n\nA rounded triangular cursor tugs a button out of the screen edge with pulsed elastic resistance.\n\nCategory: effects. Length: 6 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- An empty scene should reveal a call to action through a physical pulling gesture.\n- A button needs to feel extracted from beyond the frame with tension, recoil and release.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A cursor must accurately demonstrate an existing interface: use simulated-cursor.\n- Two complete scenes need to swap: this reveals one element rather than replacing the frame.\n\nVariables:\n- label (string): Label, default \"Create something\"\n- tension (number, 0-1.5): Tension, default 1\n- cursor_color (color): Cursor, default \"#fffaf0\"\n- color (color): Button, default \"#fffaf0\"\n- text_color (color): Text, default \"#32153c\"\n- background_color (color): Background, default \"#a800b7\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
